From dcc3edddab8ba3abdffc4fd6042f793b2bce1508 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 10:59:50 +1030
Subject: [PATCH 42/53] GE: block transfers out of a render target copied on
 the GPU too

A block transfer that copies a render target's pixels into memory no
draw renders to (a capture of the screen in main memory, as an EX Burst
makes) was only copied in guest memory, after the 1x read-back, so a
texture drawn from the copy was 1x at any internal scale. The same
rectangle is now also blitted on the GPU, at the internal scale, into a
render target standing for the destination; find_framebuffer_texture()
samples it while every byte of guest memory under the copied rectangle
is what the transfer left (a hash checked once a display list), and only
inside that rectangle. Guest memory still gets the 1x copy. A draw
recorded for frame interpolation samples a snapshot of it as of any
target. Transfers into a target the game draws to are left as before; at
most four transfer targets.

Textures over the latest 16 transfer destinations are keyed by every
byte instead of one word in 256, so a changed copy is never drawn from
an older decode.

<prefix>_NO_TRANSFER_TARGETS copies in guest memory only, as before;
<prefix>_TRANSFER_SAMPLED_KEY keys by the sampled words, as before;
<prefix>_TRACE_TRANSFERS logs each transfer and each lookup over a copy.
The census counts transfer.gpu_copy (info).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
